---
import Layout from '../../src/layouts/layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Writing about the main purpose of this blog"
	pubDate={new Date('March 26 2025')}
	heroImage="../img/about-image.jpg"
>
	<main>
		<img src="../img/about-image.jpg" alt="">
		<p>
			Alright, let me be honest with you — this isn’t a full-time travel blog. I mean, yeah, I love to travel, and yeah, I love to write about it. But this site? It’s part of something bigger.
		</p>
	
		<p>
			I’m learning to become a front-end developer. This blog is one of the ways I’m leveling up — building something real, something personal, something that doesn’t just sit in a tutorial folder collecting digital dust.
		</p>
	
		<p>
			The goal? To improve my skills and eventually build beautiful, functional websites — like this one, but even better.
		</p>
	
		<p>
			So yeah, it’s a passion project. But it’s also a playground. I’m experimenting with layouts, components, content systems, and all the little details that make a website feel alive.
		</p>
	
		<p>
			And hey — if you're reading this and thinking, "I’d love a website like this for my own project," or "I’ve got an idea but no clue where to start" — hit me up.
		</p>
		<a href="https://jpiedra.com">👉 Check out my portfolio</a>
		<p>
			Let’s build something together — whether it's your blog, your business site, or something wild and creative we dream up over coffee.
		</p>		
	</main>
</Layout>

